"""EA-MIDST-01 v1.1 draft, second pass: the Haran Gawaita read whole in Drower's translation as published by the Gnostic Society Library
(the author's copy, supplied 2026-11-11 03:56 as an .mht of the page; text extracted to ../drower/hg.txt), folded into section 13 at the
author's word ('yup lets fold that all in'). Every English quotation of the Gawaita is asserted against hg.txt; line-break hyphens and the page's space
before commas are normalized in the printed quotation, as in 13.4.   python3 apply_v11b.py   (after apply_v11.py)"""
import pathlib, re
H = pathlib.Path(__file__).parent
P = H / "EA-MIDST-01-v1.1-draft.md"; T = P.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
G = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", (H.parent / "drower/hg.txt").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
G = re.sub(r"([a-z])- ([a-z])", r"\1\2", G)
def gq(q):
    n = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", q)
    assert n in G, ("GAWAITA MISS", q); return q
def para(prefix):
    m = [x for x in re.finditer(r"(?m)^" + re.escape(prefix) + r".*$", T)]
    assert len(m) == 1, (prefix, len(m)); return m[0]
def replace_para(prefix, new):
    global T; m = para(prefix); T = T[:m.start()] + new + T[m.end():]
def after_para(prefix, new):
    global T; m = para(prefix); T = T[:m.end()] + "\n\n" + new + T[m.end():]
def sub(old, new):
    global T; assert T.count(old) == 1, (old[:70], T.count(old)); T = T.replace(old, new)
def Q(s): return '"' + re.sub(r" ([,;])", r"\1", gq(s)) + '"'

# 13.0: the text's own name for itself
sub("The text conducts itself as a confession of what happened and what it meant. Its frame is its own.",
    "It names itself: " + Q("this book - its name is the Great Revelation") + ", " + Q("the Diwan of Great Revelation called the Haran Gawaita") + ", " + Q("writing of great revelation that was given to Adam the first man") +
    ". It closes its own text against change: " + Q("alter no word or command of the great Father of Glory") + "; " + Q("removing nothing from this writing of great revelation") +
    ". The text conducts itself as a confession of what happened and what it meant, and it calls itself a revelation. Its frame is its own.")

# 13.2: now read whole
replace_para("13.2. ", "13.2. The text: Drower, *The Haran Gawaita and the Baptism of Hibil-Ziwa* (Studi e Testi 176, Vatican 1953); Burtea, *Haran Gauaita* (Harrassowitz 2020). Checked 2026-11-10 against the Drower translation as published by the Gnostic Society Library (gnosis.org/library/haran.htm, which omits Drower's footnotes; copy supplied by the author), and against the Mandaic transliteration of the Comprehensive Aramaic Lexicon, text 74501, \"Haran Gauaita\", based on DC 36 (page 1 supplied by the author). Read whole on 2026-11-11 in the same translation, from the author's saved copy of the page (5,869 words as extracted), every new English quotation in §13 asserted against it, with the page's line-break hyphens and its space before commas normalized as in 13.4. Neither the translation nor the Mandaic is seated; Drower's translation is under copyright, and the copy is held as the author's.")

# 13.6: rewritten on the whole text
replace_para("13.6. ", "13.6. The Gawaita as key to the seven stations, read whole. The Apocalypse gives its key at 1:20: \"οἱ ἑπτὰ ἀστέρες ἄγγελοι τῶν ἑπτὰ ἐκκλησιῶν εἰσίν, καὶ αἱ λυχνίαι αἱ ἑπτὰ ἑπτὰ ἐκκλησίαι εἰσίν\", seven powers each over a community. The Gawaita states the same structure twice, as history. The dark seven: Ruha and her seven sons, a House " + Q("surrounded (it by) seven walls") + " (13.4), a people " + Q("of the House of the Seven") + ", and powers that found communities: " + Q("for Mercury founded a community in Qum, and Saturn founded a community in Sinai") + ", with Ruha's own, " + Q("the city of Jerusalem amongst the community which Ruha founded") +
    ". The seven of the Life: seven guards, each installed over a place, Zazai in Baghdad, Papa on the Tigris at the mouth of the Karun, Anuš at its source, Anuš-Šaiar on the Euphrates, Brik-Yawar at Pumbdita, Njab on the mountains of Glazlak, Ska-Manda at the tail of the Parwan range, and then all seven " + Q("at the seven corners of the House , upon the seven horns of the worlds") +
    ". Seven named occupants, each over a community's place: on the Gawaita's own terms these are the seven communities, and the Apocalypse's seven messengers over seven churches are the same figure. One of the seven then departs and six remain: " + Q("the said Zazai, one of the righteous elect , rose to the firmament and abode with Yurbas sixty-two days, and ascended to his fathers; but those (other) six chosen righteous ones sent forth their descendants into the world") +
    ". Applied to the letters station by station, the Gawaita yields this.\n\n"
    "- Ephesus, Mercury. The Gawaita's Mercury is the false Messiah: " + Q("he is a false Messiah that walketh by fraud and sorcery. He is Mercury, who attracteth attention") + "; his community is at Qum, which the text glosses " + Q("Nisrat (Nazareth), a city of the Jews, which is called the city of Qum") + "; " + Q("he took to himself a people and was called by the name of the False Messiah") + ". The Ephesian station tests " + "\"τοὺς λέγοντας ἑαυτοὺς ἀποστόλους καὶ οὐκ εἰσίν, καὶ εὗρες αὐτοὺς ψευδεῖς\"" + " (2:2). The textual hook of 11.4 is the Gawaita's identification: Mercury's station is the station of the false sent.\n"
    "- Pergamum, Mars. The Gawaita's Mars goes with the Son of Slaughter: " + Q("Mars accompanieth him because he is the Seal of prophets of the Lie") + "; " + Q("he drew the sword and converted people to himself by the sword") + "; at the end the sword departs, " + Q("the sword brought by the Son of Darkness , he whose sword was of the world of Satan") + ", " + Q("until Mars came and set up his sign and bound him thereto by oath") + ". Pergamum is " + "\"ὅπου ὁ θρόνος τοῦ Σατανᾶ\"" + " (2:13), where a witness was killed, and its speaker holds the sharp two-edged sword and makes war with the sword of his mouth (2:12, 16). A sword of Satan's world, set under Mars, is answered at the Mars station by the sword of the mouth.\n"
    "- Thyatira, Venus. Ruha is Venus in the Ginza (\"Ruha d-Qudša, Estra, Libat (Venus)\", 12.1). In the Gawaita Ruha founds the community at Jerusalem, and she writes through another: sent by Adonai " + Q("disguised as Hibil-Ziwa, so as to take his judgement away from him") + ", she dwells in the ethnarch Qiqil and dictates, " + Q("I, Hibil-Ziwa, have brought parchment and reed-pen , so write a Root of Life and a Saying and a Mystery, and disseminate (them) send (them) forth") + "; " + Q("So schism ensued amongst the Nasoraeans") + ". Thyatira's charge is a woman " + "\"ἡ λέγουσα ἑαυτὴν προφῆτιν, καὶ διδάσκει καὶ πλανᾷ τοὺς ἐμοὺς δούλους πορνεῦσαι\"" + " (2:20). At the Venus station both texts have a false prophetess who teaches and leads astray; the Gawaita's teaches by dictated writing sent out to the communities, the counterfeit of the commission (§15).\n"
    "- Sardis, Saturn. Saturn founds the community at Sinai, where the False Messiah's people live: " + Q("he and his brother dwell on Mount Sinai, and he joineth all races to him") + ". Sardis has a name for being alive and is dead (3:1). The join is through #1101's \"Abandoned Sign of Seven\"; on the Gawaita's text it is a place and a founder, and the letter's condition is not named there. Moderate.\n"
    "- Smyrna and Philadelphia. The Gawaita gives Moon and Jupiter no community. The two letters with no reproach share one charge, against \"τῶν λεγόντων Ἰουδαίους εἶναι ἑαυτούς, καὶ οὐκ εἰσίν ἀλλὰ συναγωγὴ τοῦ Σατανᾶ\" (2:9) and \"τῶν λεγόντων ἑαυτοὺς Ἰουδαίους εἶναι, καὶ οὐκ εἰσὶν ἀλλὰ ψεύδονται\" (3:9); the Gawaita's charge against those it calls " + Q("of the House of the Seven") + " stands beside it. The Gawaita does not test the Moon and Jupiter assignments.\n"
    "- Laodicea, Sun. At the close the deliverer is the day of the Sun: " + Q("so that thereby Habs'aba (Sunday) may be his deliverer, and save him from the children of Krun; and I will set him at my right hand") + ". Laodicea's promise is the throne beside the speaker, \"δώσω αὐτῷ καθίσαι μετ’ ἐμοῦ ἐν τῷ θρόνῳ μου\" (3:21). At the Sun station, the last of the circuit (11.5b), both texts give the seat at the right hand.\n\n"
    "Four of the seven stations take a Gawaita identification on its own text (Ephesus, Pergamum, Thyatira, Laodicea); one takes a founder and a place (Sardis); two take a shared charge and no planet (Smyrna, Philadelphia). The Gawaita gives planetary communities to Mercury and Saturn only, and Ruha's to Venus through the Ginza's naming; it does not give each planet a community. Its seven communities are the seven stations of the guards. The Gawaita is the outside source the constraint test asks for (11.5a): profiles of the powers given by a text the archive did not write, a text that offers them as the key. Its date stands beside every line of it.")

sub("\n\n## 14. The precedent", "\n\n" + "13.7. What else the Great Revelation yields for the Apocalypse, read on its terms and dated. (i) The sealed close. The Gawaita forbids altering a word and taking anything away (13.0); the Apocalypse: \"ἐάν τις ἐπιθῇ ἐπ’ αὐτά\" and \"ἐάν τις ἀφέλῃ ἀπὸ τῶν λόγων τοῦ βιβλίου τῆς προφητείας ταύτης\" (22:18–19). The Gawaita also rules on disclosure: whoever reveals its weighty things before fools " + Q("layeth up for himself sixty causes of stumbling and sixty sins") + ", and the one who keeps silent is forgiven; the Apocalypse seals the seven thunders and unseals its prophecy (10:4; 22:10). (ii) The eighth of the seven. The end goes to " + Q("Mamit daughter of Qin , the mother of the Seven (what ) occupied seven portions, and the eighth was given to Amamit as hers") + ", in " + Q("this is the eighth world") + "; the Apocalypse's beast \"αὐτὸς ὄγδοός ἐστιν καὶ ἐκ τῶν ἑπτά ἐστιν\" (17:11). (iii) Forty-two. The Gawaita's Yahia-Yuhana teaches in the fallen House, " + Q("Forty-two years (he dwelt) therein") + ", the number the Ginza gives his baptizing (12.3); the Apocalypse's holy city is trampled and the beast has authority \"μῆνας τεσσεράκοντα δύο\" (11:2; 13:5). (iv) The crowned envoy. The child is crowned and seated beside the one who sends him, " + Q("he set the crown on him and seated him beside himself") + ", and is called " + Q("envoy of the High King of Light") + " and " + Q("the apostle") + "; he dwells at Jerusalem. (v) The counterfeit commission. Ruha's dictated writings, sent out, divide the communities; Qiqil recants and burns them, and " + Q("some of those writings remained with them") + " (13.6, Thyatira). The Apocalypse commands true writing and its sending (15.1) and tests the false sent (2:2). Each is a parallel offered by the Gawaita's own frame; none is a claim of dependence in either direction, since the Gawaita is copied in the Arab era and speaks of the Son of Slaughter (13.4)." + "\n\n## 14. The precedent")

sub("whether the Haran Gawaita gives a community to each of the seven (13.6);", "the Haran Gawaita's planetary communities beyond Mercury, Saturn and Ruha's, which its text does not give (13.6);")
